Allow building with C++26.

 - Enable c++26 in CMakeLists.txt
 - std::is_trivial is deprecated in C++26.  Use
   std::is_trivially_default_constructible and std::is_trivially_copyable
   instead.

 - This code:

```
      const std::vector<std::string>& v = ...;
      ... = std::ranges::find (v, "foo");
```

   works with C++23 but not with C++26.  The second type here is an array,
   and array equality comparison was deprecated in C++20 and removed in C++26.
